WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:19.422
One quiet afternoon, something extraordinary happened.

2
00:00:19.423 --> 00:00:25.598
"Snort, snort, OOOOOOOOOOIIIIINNK, snort," cried the little pig.

3
00:00:25.599 --> 00:00:28.722
He seemed to be in pain.

4
00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:33.019
"Why don't you look after your animals?" Sarah shouted.

5
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.091
"What's the matter, Gub-Gub?" Dr. Dolittle asked.

6
00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:40.539
"He ate something bad, of course," Sarah said.

7
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:49.050
"No, he hurt his foot," the doctor said.

8
00:00:49.051 --> 00:00:52.571
"How did you know that?" Sarah asked.

9
00:00:52.572 --> 00:00:56.847
"Well, I think Gub-Gub told me," he answered.

10
00:00:56.848 --> 00:01:00.233
"Are you out of your mind?" she shouted.

11
00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:07.582
"Animals can't talk!"

12
00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:12.330
"Maybe I am crazy," Dr. Dolittle said to himself.

13
00:01:12.331 --> 00:01:13.935
"No, you're not.

14
00:01:13.936 --> 00:01:18.778
You're talking to me right now!" Polynesia pointed out.

15
00:01:18.779 --> 00:01:25.166
"But you're a parrot," the doctor replied.

16
00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:29.011
"You understood Gub-Gub," Polynesia continued.

17
00:01:29.012 --> 00:01:33.457
"But that's impossible!" Dr. Dolittle sat up.

18
00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:38.171
"Dr. Dolittle, you have the gift," the parrot said.

19
00:01:38.172 --> 00:01:41.006
"What gift?" the doctor asked.

20
00:01:41.007 --> 00:01:46.909
"You can understand animal language," she answered.

21
00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:50.636
Dr. Dolittle was very excited.

22
00:01:50.637 --> 00:01:55.596
"I didn't know animals have their own language!" he said to Polynesia.

23
00:01:55.597 --> 00:01:57.188
"Most humans don't.

24
00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:03.324
But animals speak to each other just like people do," she said.

25
00:02:03.325 --> 00:02:06.686
"Animals also talk to people all the time.

26
00:02:06.687 --> 00:02:12.086
'I'm HUNGRY!' 'I don't want to play!' 'I'm HUNGRY!'

27
00:02:12.087 --> 00:02:13.998
'Oh, look at the yarn!

28
00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:17.125
Jump, Muffin! Jump, kitty!'

29
00:02:17.126 --> 00:02:24.313
'Meow, Meow, Meow'"

30
00:02:24.314 --> 00:02:29.503
"Then why can't people learn animal language?" Dr. Dolittle asked.

31
00:02:29.504 --> 00:02:35.051
"Only those who truly love animals can learn it," nodded Polynesia.

32
00:02:35.052 --> 00:02:40.761
"Yes, I do love animals very much," admitted the doctor.

33
00:02:40.762 --> 00:02:46.654
Every day, Dr. Dolittle studied the animal language with Polynesia's help.

34
00:02:46.655 --> 00:02:51.582
"Animals don't always talk with words," Polynesia whispered.

35
00:02:51.583 --> 00:03:00.917
"We can speak with our eyes, our tails, our feet . . . with everything.

36
00:03:00.918 --> 00:03:03.754
What do you think Jip is saying?"

37
00:03:03.755 --> 00:03:07.484
"It looks like he is playing," the doctor answered.

38
00:03:07.485 --> 00:03:09.954
Polynesia shook her head.

39
00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:12.169
"But what he's really saying is:

40
00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:16.884
'Get off my back, you annoying flea!'"

41
00:03:16.885 --> 00:03:20.343
It wasn't easy to learn the animal language.

42
00:03:20.344 --> 00:03:23.712
Dr. Dolittle made many mistakes.

43
00:03:23.713 --> 00:03:29.464
"This one wants to live in the garden, but the other one doesn't," the doctor observed.

44
00:03:29.465 --> 00:03:35.522
"Listen more carefully, Doctor," said Polynesia.

45
00:03:35.523 --> 00:03:38.697
"Squeak, squeak, JEEEEEEEEEEEPPPPPP!

46
00:03:38.698 --> 00:03:42.392
Jeep, Jeep, squeakkkkk!" cried one mouse.

47
00:03:42.393 --> 00:03:45.943
"OH!" the doctor shouted excitedly.

48
00:03:45.944 --> 00:03:49.656
"He stepped on her feet so she's angry with him!"

49
00:03:49.657 --> 00:03:56.314
"That's right! And he didn't even say sorry!" squeaked the mouse.

50
00:03:56.315 --> 00:04:01.713
Soon Dr. Dolittle could speak and understand the animal language perfectly.

51
00:04:01.714 --> 00:04:06.478
"Oh, please, someone help me," the horse cried.

52
00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:11.951
"I'll help you," Dr. Dolittle gently answered.

53
00:04:11.952 --> 00:04:15.631
"You can speak our language?" the horse whispered.

54
00:04:15.632 --> 00:04:21.114
"Yes. Now tell me what the problem is," said the doctor.

55
00:04:21.115 --> 00:04:28.784
"I'm so thirsty and hot, but the old man won't give me any water!" complained the horse.

56
00:04:28.785 --> 00:04:33.486
"You can have some water from my garden," Dr. Dolittle offered.

57
00:04:33.487 --> 00:04:37.701
"You seem to understand animals," the old man said.

58
00:04:37.702 --> 00:04:43.491
"You should be an animal doctor."
